/E (The harbour was crowded with passengers, servants, and trunks this morning, though our first-class arrangements spared us much of the confusion faced by ordinary travellers. Even amidst the disorder, I could not help but admire how steam travel now connects Europe with such speed and regularity for gentlemen of means.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
