/E (In reflecting upon these journeys, I am struck by how greatly travel is shaped not only by place, but by class, labour, gender, and circumstance. The wealthy traveller experiences Europe through comfort, leisure, and opportunity, while the labouring man sees the same ports and streets through work and hardship.)
